  "readmeFile": "build\\native\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.11.0: phnt sync to 2a0045bfc\n\nSync Veil headers to phnt commit 2a0045bfc572d1c9ea6d8843dc6cf6cae1e20fd7.\nCovers both unreleased sync ranges, a284c82c9f0fd6afb1b7c215ad17fedd95d3525e and\n2a0045bfc572d1c9ea6d8843dc6cf6cae1e20fd7.\n\nFrom a284c82c9f0fd6afb1b7c215ad17fedd95d3525e:\n\n- AGENTS: define source auditing, API conversion, version mapping, validation, and cache cleanup policy\n- D3DKMT: add NTSYSAPI exports for process enumeration helpers\n- Executive: update delay semantics, system information metadata, code-integrity structures, OSL RAM-disk address type, and Nt/Zw NLS signatures\n- Etw: add PCW counter APIs and helpers plus byte-packed TCP/UDP WMI event layouts\n- Loader: add the 32-bit LDRP_DEPENDENCY representation\n- PowerManager: reconcile energy-tracker limits, flags, fields, ordering, and record offsets\n- Win32: add GDI handle limits, pseudo-window ownership, message-pump, low-latency, and capture-buffer declarations; update FN_DISPATCH\n- Zw declarations: normalize IRQL, NTSYSAPI, and NTAPI metadata with documented WDK kernel-mode adaptations\n\nFrom 2a0045bfc572d1c9ea6d8843dc6cf6cae1e20fd7:\n\n- ALPC: add ALPC_HANDLEFLG_INDIRECT and ALPC_INDIRECT_HANDLE_MAX, rebuild the ALPC_HANDLE_ATTR32 and ALPC_HANDLE_ATTR layouts as unions with bitfields\n- Etw: add the byte-packed TCP/IP send-event layouts and connection-id/sequence fields, correct the UDP transfer-size width, add the PCW buffer structures and parsing helpers\n- Executive: rename BOOT_ENTROPY_NT_RESULT.maxEntropySources, document the WHEA IPMI fields, fix the Nt/Zw NLS declarations\n- Loader: correct the LdrControlFlowGuardEnforced guard and its documentation, keeping the Windows 10 baseline guard instead of the upstream RS3 threshold\n- ObjectManager: add OBJECT_SET_REF_TRACE_INFORMATION\n- Process: name the leap-second flag, union the global-flag and extended-feature-disable fields in PEB and TEB, move NtContinue after NtContinueEx\n- RuntimeLibrary: define the RTL_RCU structures with their prototypes, add the RtlIsZeroMemory inline implementation, relax the locale file-mapping output parameter\n- veil-update skill: map ntpebteb.h and ntxcapi.h, treat ntmisc.h as multi-domain, align the version token conversions with the synchronization policy\n\nBREAKING CHANGE:\n\n- BOOT_ENTROPY_NT_RESULT.maxEntropySources renamed to MaxEntropySources\n- ALPC_HANDLE_ATTR is now a union of bitfields: SameAccess, SameAttributes, Indirect, Inherit, GrantedAccess and the reserved members are no longer directly addressable, and ALPC_HANDLE_ATTR32 drops its duplicated fields\n- RTL_RCU_COOKIE is removed; RtlRcuReadLock takes PRTL_RCU_THREAD_ENTRY*, RtlRcuReadUnlock takes it by value, and RtlRcuFree and RtlRcuSynchronize return VOID\n- NtGetNlsSectionPtr, NtInitializeNlsFiles and RtlGetLocaleFileMappingAddress change their parameters and annotations, and the Zw declarations follow\n- WMI TCP/IP and UDP event structures are byte-packed and carry connection-id and sequence fields; WMI_UDP_V4 and WMI_UDP_V6 TransferSize widened to ULONG\n- PEB.NtGlobalFlag2 is now a bitfield struct; the raw value is PEB.NtGlobalFlags2\n- LdrControlFlowGuardEnforced stays available on the whole Windows 10 baseline in Veil, narrower than the current upstream guard",
